# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12: Counter's body calls mk, which throws Oops, and does not catch it; a
# procedure has no header to list it in, so the rule of every callable (book §14) refuses the call.
fn: mk () int
    throws: Oops
    if: 1 = 1
        throw: Oops(5)
    return: 1
end: mk
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    int: v 0
    v: mk()
return
Counter
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
